NNAAMMEE
       pbmtopsg3 - convert PBM images to Postscript with G3 fax compression


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppbbmmttooppssgg33 [----ttiittllee==_t_i_t_l_e] [----ddppii==_d_p_i] [_f_i_l_e_s_p_e_c]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppbbmmttooppssgg33  converts  the PBM images in the input PBM file to pages in a
       Postscript file encoded with G3 fax compression.

       ppnnmmttooppss is a more general program for converting from the  Netpbm  for‐
       mats  to  Postscript, though it cannot produce the particular subformat
       that ppbbmmttooppssgg33 does.

       If you don't specify _f_i_l_e_s_p_e_c, the input is from Standard Input.

       Remember that you can create a multi-image PBM file simply by  concate‐
       nating  single-image PBM files, so if each page is in a different file,
       you might do:

       cat faxpage* | pbmtopsg3 >fax.ps



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppbbmmttooppssgg33 recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --ttiittllee The Postscript title value.  Default is no title.


       --ddppii   The resolution of the Postscript output.  Default is 72 dpi.




